+<!-- rnb-text-begin -->
+<div id="assigning-cell-type-identity-to-clusters" class="section level2">
+<h2>Assigning cell type identity to clusters</h2>
+<p>At a coarse level, we can use canonical markers to match the unbiased clustering to known cell types:</p>
+<!-- rnb-text-end -->
+<!-- rnb-chunk-begin -->
+<!-- rnb-source-begin  -->
+<pre class="r"><code># stash current cluster IDs
+tiss &lt;- StashIdent(object = tiss, save.name = &quot;cluster.ids&quot;)
+# enumerate current cluster IDs and the labels for them
+cluster.ids &lt;- c(0, 1)
+free_annotation &lt;- c(&quot;cell type 1&quot;, &quot;cell type 2&quot;)
+cell_ontology_class &lt;-c(&quot;ontology class 1&quot;, &quot;ontology class 2&quot;)
+stash_annotations(tiss, cluster.ids, free_annotation, cell_ontology_class)</code></pre>
+<!-- rnb-source-end -->
